    {'id':'y3-t2-w3-l1','year':'Y3','term':'T2',     'week':3,'weekLesson':1,     'sequence':'Sequence 2','lesson':'Lesson 1',     'focus':'adding the -ly suffix',     'explanation':'For most root words, we simply add the -ly suffix (because it begins with a consonant). However, there are some exceptions to this, where other rules apply. If the root word ends in y, change y to i before adding -ly. For example, the word happy becomes happily. If the root word ends in -le, change -le to -ly. For example, the word gentle becomes gently. If the root word ends in -ic, use the -ally suffix (instead of -ly). For example, the word magic becomes magically.',     'hlWords':['kind', 'kindly', 'certain', 'certainly', 'ideal', 'ideally', 'month', 'monthly', 'real', 'really', 'complete', 'completely', 'friend', 'friendly', 'coward', 'cowardly', 'general', 'generally', 'likely', 'shortly', 'finally']},
