    {'id':'y3-t4-w1-l1','year':'Y3','term':'T4',     'week':1,'weekLesson':1,     'sequence':'Sequence 4','lesson':'Lesson 1',     'focus':'words ending -sion',     'explanation':'The -sion ending is applied to verbs to form nouns. The -sion ending sounds like zh-un. When a verb ends in se, we can remove se and replace it with sion. For example, the verb confuse can be used to form the noun confusion. When a verb ends in de, we can remove de and replace it with sion. For example, the verb decide can be used to form the noun decision.',     'hlWords':['version', 'confusion', 'revision', 'fusion', 'television', 'verse', 'confuse', 'revise', 'fuse', 'televise', 'averse', 'aversion', 'disperse', 'dispersion', 'diffuse', 'diffusion', 'precise', 'precision', 'converse', 'conversion', 'supervise', 'supervision']},
