    {'id':'y3-t6-w4-l1','year':'Y3','term':'T6',     'week':4,'weekLesson':1,     'sequence':'Mastery 6','lesson':'Lesson 1',     'focus':'alternative long a sounds',     'explanation':'The long a sound has various representations. In this sequence, children are introduced to the following graphemes – ei / eigh / ey. The ei grapheme is often found in the middle of a word. Examples include rein, beige and veil. The ey grapheme is often found at the end of a word. Examples include grey, obey and survey. The eigh grapheme can be found in different positions within words. The most common roots that use this grapheme include eight, weigh and neigh. These roots form many other words containing the same grapheme (e.g. eighteen and neighbour).',     'hlWords':['beige', 'eight', 'they', 'vein', 'neigh', 'obey', 'reindeer', 'weight', 'survey', 'weigh', 'veil', 'convey', 'neighbour']},
    {'id':'y3-t6-w4-l2','year':'Y3','term':'T6',     'week':4,'weekLesson':2,     'sequence':'Mastery 6','lesson':'Lesson 2',     'focus':'alternative long a sounds',     'explanation':'The long a sound has various representations. In this sequence, children are introduced to the following graphemes – ei / eigh / ey. The ei grapheme is often found in the middle of a word. Examples include rein, beige and veil. The ey grapheme is often found at the end of a word. Examples include grey, obey and survey. The eigh grapheme can be found in different positions within words. The most common roots that use this grapheme include eight, weigh and neigh. These roots form many other words containing the same grapheme (e.g. eighteen and neighbour).',     'hlWords':['obey', 'veil', 'grey', 'eighty', 'neighbour', 'survey', 'beige', 'convey', 'reindeer', 'veins', 'prey', 'eighteen']},
