    {'id':'y4-t4-w4-l1','year':'Y4','term':'T4',     'week':4,'weekLesson':1,     'sequence':'Sequence 6','lesson':'Lesson 1',     'focus':'prefixes',     'explanation':'Prefixes are units of meaning added to the beginning of a root word in order to change its meaning. The re- prefix usually means again. For example, the word rewrite means to write again. It can, in some cases, mean back. For example, the word retreat means to move back. The sub- prefix means under. For example, the word subheading means a heading underneath the main heading. These prefixes are usually added with no change to the root word.',     'hlWords':['recreate', 'submarine', 'reschedule', 'reprint', 'subheading', 'redecorate', 'submerge', 'rewrite', 'reappear', 'autograph']},
    {'id':'y4-t4-w4-l2','year':'Y4','term':'T4',     'week':4,'weekLesson':2,     'sequence':'Sequence 6','lesson':'Lesson 2',     'focus':'prefixes',     'explanation':'Prefixes are units of meaning added to the beginning of a root word in order to change its meaning. The super- prefix means above or beyond. It is used to show that something is better than or superior to something else. For example, the word superglue means glue that is above or better/stronger than other glue. The inter- prefix means between. For example, the word intercity means something is happening between more than one city. These prefixes are usually added with no change to the root word.',     'hlWords':['interconnect', 'superpower', 'intercity', 'supermarket', 'interlink', 'interact', 'superstar', 'superhero', 'subheading', 'reappear']},
    {'id':'y4-t4-w4-l3','year':'Y4','term':'T4',     'week':4,'weekLesson':3,     'sequence':'Sequence 6','lesson':'Lesson 3',     'focus':'prefixes',     'explanation':'Prefixes are units of meaning added to the beginning of a root word in order to change its meaning. The anti- prefix means against or the opposite. For example, the word antigravity means a force that works against gravity. The auto- prefix means self or own. For example, the word autobiography means a biography (life story) written about yourself. These prefixes are usually added with no change to the root word.',     'hlWords':['antibacterial', 'antivirus', 'autograph', 'antisocial', 'autobiography', 'antihero', 'anticlockwise', 'antigravity', 'subheading', 'reappear']},
