    {'id':'y4-t5-w5-l1','year':'Y4','term':'T5',     'week':5,'weekLesson':1,     'sequence':'Sequence 9','lesson':'Lesson 1',     'focus':'uh spelled ou',     'explanation':'This sequence focuses on words containing the uh (/ʌ/) sound spelled ou. These words do not follow a clear spelling rule. Instead, they simply have to be learned. However, this sequence explores common placement of the uh sound spelled ou. For example, the uh sound spelled ou sometimes appears after the letter c. Example words include couple, country, cousin and courage. Similarly, the uh sound spelled ou sometimes appears before ble/ple at the end of a word. Example words include couple, double and trouble.',     'hlWords':['young', 'trouble', 'couple', 'cousins', 'country', 'courage', 'touch', 'cousin', 'double', 'nourish']},
