    {'id':'y5-t3-w1-l1','year':'Y5','term':'T3',     'week':1,'weekLesson':1,     'sequence':'Sequence 4','lesson':'Lesson 1',     'focus':'the ough letter string',     'explanation':"The 'ough' letter string is a quadgraph, meaning it is a grapheme constructed from four letters.\nThere are not many words that contain this letter string and it represents a range of different sounds; therefore, these words simply need to be learned.\nThe 'ough' letter string generally makes the following sounds:\n- uff (as in enough)\n- off (as in cough)\n- aw (as in bought)\n- oa (as in although)\n- ow (as in bough)\n- oo (as in through)\n- uh (as in thorough)",     'hlWords':['rough', 'tough', 'trough', 'cough', 'enough', 'through', 'bought', 'brought', 'dough', 'plough']},
