    {'id':'y5-t4-w3-l1','year':'Y5','term':'T4',     'week':3,'weekLesson':1,     'sequence':'Sequence 5','lesson':'Lesson 7',     'focus':'silent letters',     'explanation':'There are many potential silent letters that children may come across.\nHowever, this sequence explores some of the most common ones – and the most common positions in which they occur.\nThe most common rules are as follows:\n1. The silent letter b often follows the letter m at the end of a word (e.g. thumb).\n2. The silent letter k often precedes the letter n at the start of a word (e.g. knight).\n3. The silent letter h often follows the letter w at the start of a word (e.g. white).\n4. The silent letter w often precedes the letter r at the start of a word (e.g. wrong).\n5. The silent letter n often follows the letter m at the end of a word (e.g. autumn).\n6. The silent letter g often precedes the letter n at the start of a word (e.g. gnome) or at the end of a word (e.g. design).\n7. The silent letter t often comes between s and le (e.g. castle) or precedes en at the end of a word (e.g. listen).',     'hlWords':['jostle', 'hasten', 'apostle', 'glisten', 'rustle', 'soften', 'nestle', 'whistle', 'listen', 'castle', 'thistle', 'fasten']},
    {'id':'y5-t4-w3-l2','year':'Y5','term':'T4',     'week':3,'weekLesson':2,     'sequence':'Sequence 5','lesson':'Lesson 8',     'focus':'silent letters',     'explanation':'In the final two lessons in this sequence, children explore other, less common, silent letters.\n1. The silent letter u after the letter g – at the start of a word (e.g. guard).\n2. The silent letter s after the letter i (e.g. island).\n3. The silent letter h before the letter o (e.g. honest).\n4. The silent letter b before the letter t (e.g. subtle).\nThey also revisit this rule:\nThe silent letter t often comes between s and le (e.g. castle) or precedes en at the end of a word (e.g. listen).',     'hlWords':['hourglass', 'subtle', 'guarantee', 'viscount', 'guitar', 'hour', 'guess', 'doubt', 'guilty', 'ghost', 'honesty', 'island', 'guardian', 'guard']},
